The  driver supports the ATI Technologies IXP IDE controller, and
provides the interface with the hardware  for  the  driver.   The
0x0002  flag  forces  the  driver  to disable DMA on chipsets for
which DMA would normally be enabled.  This can be used as  a  de‐
bugging  aid, or to work around problems where the IDE controller
is wired up to the system incorrectly.  The  supported  IDE  con‐
trollers  are  ATI  SB200  ATI  SB300 ATI SB400, Parallel ATA ATI
SB400, Serial ATA ATI SB700, Serial and Parallel ATA  Some  SB700
controllers  can hang under load when Native IDE mode is selected
in the system BIOS, but work fine in AHCI mode.
